.TH "bead manifest dry-run" 1  "bead manifest dry-run " 
.SH NAME
bead manifest dry\-run \- Report a manifest\*(Aqs full semantic delta without mutating anything
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead manifest dry\-run\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-input\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate and execute a manifest inside one transaction that is
always rolled back.
.PP
The report is exact: document validation failures, not\-found targets,
transition refusals, revision and lease guards, and cycle detection all fire
against the same pinned snapshot a commit would run on, so a dry\-run that
succeeds commits. Nothing is written: no event is appended durably, no
sequence advances, no checkpoint generation is published. Created IDs in the
report are provisional \-\- only a commit\*(Aqs result map carries real IDs;
correlate through the create\*(Aqs local_id.
.PP
  bead manifest dry\-run \-\-input plan.json
  bead manifest dry\-run \-\-input plan.json \-\-format json
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR
Path to the manifest JSON file
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format: text or json
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
